<title>BELGIUM: Union Miniere reopens at 3,445 bfr/shr.</title>
<headline>Union Miniere reopens at 3,445 bfr/shr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Belgian non-ferrous metals group Union Miniere SA (UM) reopened at 3,445 francs after trade was suspended ahead of the sale of a major block of UM stock.</p>
<p>The share was down nine percent at 3,410 before the suspension.</p>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) said earlier it sold 24 percent of UM to institutional investors.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
